From: Deyan Petrov <25847560+deyanp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 12:13:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] fix(elero): demote CC1101 health log from WARN to VERBOSE
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`check_health()` logged its health line unconditionally at `ESP_LOGW` on every
`RADIO_WATCHDOG_INTERVAL` (5 s), so a healthy radio produced a warning every
five seconds:

  health: MARCSTATE=0x0d RSSI=-99 dBm (raw=0xcd)

MARCSTATE 0x0d is RX — the expected idle state — and the function returns
`RadioHealth::OK` immediately afterwards, so nothing is wrong when this fires.
The preceding comment ("Log RSSI for TX hardware test") suggests it is leftover
bring-up instrumentation that kept its bring-up log level.

Only that line changes. The genuine warnings that follow — RX FIFO overflow,
stuck in IDLE, unexpected MARCSTATE — keep `ESP_LOGW`, so a real fault is now
visible instead of buried in one healthy line per 5 s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J12Zptv6PA4jU97du7vmxZ
(cherry picked from commit f4a4912773b9ebd0111022ecc79143a1ecf923da)
---
 components/elero/cc1101_driver.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/elero/cc1101_driver.cpp b/components/elero/cc1101_driver.cpp
index 37e1ef5..f3cf6d0 100644
--- a/components/elero/cc1101_driver.cpp
+++ b/components/elero/cc1101_driver.cpp
@@ -162,7 +162,7 @@ RadioHealth CC1101Driver::check_health() {
   // Log RSSI for TX hardware test (read CC1101 RSSI register in RX mode)
   uint8_t rssi_raw = this->read_status(CC1101_RSSI);
   int16_t rssi_dbm = (rssi_raw >= 128) ? ((rssi_raw - 256) / 2 - 74) : (rssi_raw / 2 - 74);
-  ESP_LOGW(TAG, "health: MARCSTATE=0x%02x RSSI=%d dBm (raw=0x%02x)", marc, rssi_dbm, rssi_raw);
+  ESP_LOGV(TAG, "health: MARCSTATE=0x%02x RSSI=%d dBm (raw=0x%02x)", marc, rssi_dbm, rssi_raw);
 
   // RX is the expected idle state
   if (marc == CC1101_MARCSTATE_RX) {
